  "premise_review": [
    "boolSystem is the identity-step PUnit-input/PUnit-resolution Boolean system. boolPresentation has the True invariant and a name/version. Those metadata and process-interface fields are not promoted as maintained Math components.",
    "boolFlip complements both state and observed Boolean value. Identity step/observation and True invariant discharge its three presentation-homomorphism laws. Its nonidentity theorem evaluates the mapState field at true; no abstract classification of endomorphisms is asserted.",
    "boolFlipReaction applies the same complement at every cell of the constant triangle; its naturality law uses identity contracts and Presentation.Hom.ext. The first anonymous example is exactly a field projection, with arbitrary m,n,op,x retained.",
    "nonNaturalTrianglePatch complements only the top cell while retaining identity boundary replacement maps. firstTriangleFace is specifically delta(0:Fin3), a proper 1-to-2 boundary operator. The mismatch stores expected=id and actual=boolFlip with explicit equality and inequality evidence.",
    "The two negative anonymous examples use the imported mismatch not_boundaryCompatible and not_extendsTo lemmas. They concern this specific patch, not every local update or every fabric.",
    "emptyShape is a constant Empty-valued simplicial object. emptyFabric and emptyCompleteFiller discharge every field by cell.elim; no cell or nonempty filler is constructed and no choice is invoked by these exact proof bodies.",
    "The final equivalence quantifies over a cell : emptyFabric.Cell n and a patch at that cell, an impossible index for this empty fixture. It uses the explicit emptyCompleteFiller; no unconditional BoundaryCompatible-to-ExtendsTo theorem for arbitrary fabrics is supplied.",
    "All four anonymous examples, named commands, original namespaces/opens, docs and proofs remain byte-exact in both pinned archives. Filename/replay location is not an execution result; no replay, elaboration or mathematical acceptance is asserted."
  ],
